WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:05.438
The 2020 election was a stunning rebuke to&nbsp;prohibitionists and a crucial milestone in&nbsp;the unraveling

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.044
of the disastrous U.S.&nbsp;War on Drugs. 

00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:13.936
Across the country and by overwhelming margins, American voters came out in favor of legalizing marijuana,  

00:00:13.936 --> 00:00:19.326
removing criminal penalties for psychedelic use, and opening new possibilities for treating drug addiction

00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:20.732
as a public health concern.

00:00:20.732 --> 00:00:24.822
The biggest victory was in Oregon,&nbsp;where voters overwhelmingly approved a measure 

00:00:24.822 --> 00:00:31.492
that will make it the first state to eliminate the&nbsp;possibility of jail time for possession of heroin, cocaine, oxycodone,

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:32.951
and every other narcotic.

00:00:32.951 --> 00:00:38.558
Instead, those possessing small amounts of&nbsp;drugs could be hit with at most a $100 fine.

00:00:38.558 --> 00:00:40.268
It's a really bold experiment.

00:00:40.268 --> 00:00:48.473
It essentially embodies this idea that, look,&nbsp;arresting people and locking them up for&nbsp;using drugs is not very effective.

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:56.119
So let's stop&nbsp;arresting and putting them in prison, and instead&nbsp;set up education treatment recovery programs,

00:00:56.119 --> 00:01:00.723
use&nbsp;the money from the legal marijuana market to fund&nbsp;all of that.

00:01:00.723 --> 00:01:05.200
It's the harm reduction approach&nbsp;written into law, across the board.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.379
Oregon also passed Measure 109, making it&nbsp;the first state to legalize psilocybin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.379 --> 00:01:13.186
the main psychoactive&nbsp;ingredient in magic mushrooms.

00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:18.800
In 2018, the Food and Drug Administration granted&nbsp;psilocybin “breakthrough therapy” status

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.626
for treatment-resistant depression.

00:01:20.626 --> 00:01:27.143
In Washington, D.C., voters opted by a margin&nbsp;of 3 to 1 to require that law enforcement&nbsp;make the prosecution of use,

00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:33.901
possession, and&nbsp;cultivation, of entheogenic plants and fungi,&nbsp;like psilocybin mushrooms, its lowest priority.&nbsp;

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:39.060
The most important thing to keep&nbsp;in mind is it is a referendum in the sort of&nbsp;classic sense.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:45.075
It does not change law in any&nbsp;way. It simply says, "Look, government of DC:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:52.417
we, the people, think that the police&nbsp;and the district attorneys should stop&nbsp;arresting and prosecuting people

00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:55.200
for psychedelic plants. So please do that.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.626
Mississippi, Arizona, South Dakota,&nbsp;New Jersey, and Montana all passed&nbsp;initiatives 

00:02:00.626 --> 00:02:05.120
allowing marijuana to be sold&nbsp;for either medical or recreational use.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.592
Moore says that there’s a danger that some of the&nbsp;legal structures established by these ballot measures, 

00:02:10.592 --> 00:02:14.214
such as in Arizona,&nbsp;will repeat the mistakes of other states, 

00:02:14.214 --> 00:02:16.320
where regulated cartels dominate.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:22.724
It really is designed to give the existing medical&nbsp;marijuana providers control of the market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.724 --> 00:02:26.646
 and not let anybody else into the market, which is&nbsp;kind of crazy.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:32.000
It also establishes all kinds of rules governing the market that have been&nbsp; pretty well shown in other states

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.145
not to work very well. 

00:02:33.145 --> 00:02:37.411
So on the one hand, it&nbsp;legalizes marijuana. On the other hand,&nbsp;it sets up a market

00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:42.000
that is destined to be full&nbsp;of problems and corruption and crony nonsense.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.866
But, so far, a clear take away from the 2020&nbsp;election

00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:50.353
is that the American public has had enough of the government locking people in&nbsp;cages

00:02:50.353 --> 00:02:53.692
for putting mind altering substances  into their own bodies.

00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:58.393
 And the tragic War on Drugs is finally coming to an end. 

